// ─── Scale anchor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Everything this script draws is a line/box/label, and drawing objects contribute
// nothing to a pane's autoscale. With no scalable data TradingView is free to hand
// the indicator its own price scale, which then fits itself to the drawings: the
// levels stop tracking the candles and ride the viewport instead. A fully
// transparent close keeps the script welded to the chart's own range. display.pane
// keeps it out of the legend and price scale.
plot(close, "", color = color.new(color.black, 100), display = display.pane, editable = false)

//═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
//═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
fillBull = fuT10S or fuT15S or fuT30S or fuT1 or fuT2 or fuT3 or fuT4 or fuT5 or fuT6 or fuT10 or fuT12 or fuT15 or fuT20 or fuT30 or fuT45 or fuT60 or fuT120 or fuT180 or fuT240 or fuT360 or fuT480 or fuT720 or fuTD or fuTW or fuTM
fillBear = fdT10S or fdT15S or fdT30S or fdT1 or fdT2 or fdT3 or fdT4 or fdT5 or fdT6 or fdT10 or fdT12 or fdT15 or fdT20 or fdT30 or fdT45 or fdT60 or fdT120 or fdT180 or fdT240 or fdT360 or fdT480 or fdT720 or fdTD or fdTW or fdTM

alertcondition(fillBull, "Bullish imbalance filled", "Price retraced down into a higher-timeframe bullish distal edge")
alertcondition(fillBear, "Bearish imbalance filled", "Price retraced up into a higher-timeframe bearish distal edge")
